# Archive Output Location

All QAG offline build artifacts belong in **`/data/tyewhong/qag/`**:

- **`.tar`** — Docker image exports, rootfs archives
- **`.tar.gz`** — code bundles, model stores
- **`.sha256`** — checksum sidecars for any of the above

## Scripts (defaults)

- `scripts/make_qag_bundle.sh` → `QAG_ARCHIVE_DIR` (default above)
- `scripts/make_offline_tarballs.sh` → `QAG_OFFLINE_OUT` (defaults to same dir)
- `scripts/save_vllm_qwen35_image.sh` → `OUT_DIR` / `QAG_ARCHIVE_DIR`
- `scripts/migrate_archive_dir.sh` → one-time legacy path migration

Set in `.env`: `QAG_ARCHIVE_DIR=/data/tyewhong/qag`

## Retirement folder (`zz_old_qag/`)

Under **`/data/tyewhong/qag/zz_old_qag/`**, park archives that are not needed
for the **active** profile on this host:

- Active profile bundles stay in the **root** of `QAG_ARCHIVE_DIR`.
- Superseded, duplicate, or other-profile archives (e.g. ollama, kubeflow,
  legacy vLLM images) → **move** into `zz_old_qag/` — do not delete unless
  the user explicitly asks.
- `setup_offline.sh` searches `ARCHIVE_DIR` root only; retired files are not
  auto-discovered. To deploy ollama/kubeflow later, move (or symlink) the
  needed files back to the archive root.

## Legacy path (deprecated)

**`/data/tyewhong/qagredo/`** must not receive new archives. If `.tar` /
`.tar.gz` / `.sha256` files exist only there, **move** them to
`/data/tyewhong/qag/` (use `mv` on the same filesystem — do not copy ~200 GB).

Rename qagredo-prefixed bundles on move so `setup_offline.sh` finds them:

| Legacy name | Canonical name |
|-------------|----------------|
| `qagredo_bundle.tar.gz` | `qag_bundle.tar.gz` |
| `qagredo-v1.tar` | `qag-v1.tar` |
| `qagredo-kubeflow.tar` | `qag-kubeflow.tar` |
| `qagredo-vllm_qwen35-localcuda.rootfs.tar` | `vllm-qwen35-localcuda.rootfs.tar` |

(Include matching `.sha256` sidecars. Other `models_*` archives move as-is.)

Dry-run: `bash scripts/migrate_archive_dir.sh`  
Apply: `bash scripts/migrate_archive_dir.sh --execute`

## Agent behavior

- Never delete or truncate archives under `/data/tyewhong/qag/` or
  `/data/tyewhong/qag/zz_old_qag/` unless the user explicitly requests it
  (see `safe-deletion-guardrails.mdc`).
- Never write new `.tar` / `.tar.gz` archives to `/data/tyewhong/qagredo/`.
- Never leave `.tar` / `.tar.gz` in `/home/tyewhong/qag/` or `offline_out/`
  after building; move or write directly to `/data/tyewhong/qag/`.
- When giving manual `docker save` or `tar czf` commands, use
  `/data/tyewhong/qag/` as the output directory.
- `.zip` archives are not covered by this rule (may live next to datasets,
  e.g. pathfinder).
